# Tutorial 12 — Best Practices
# Naming, structure, common bugs, and the habits that keep projects maintainable.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_tutorial_12_best_practices
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}
{{BG_DECL}}@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[set ui.textBoxAsset none]
[set ui.continueIndicator spinning_arrow]
[if tutorial_still]
[set ui.reduceMotion true]
[else]
[set ui.reduceMotion false]
[endif]
[if !tutorial_initialized]
[set tutorial_count 0]
[flag tutorial_initialized]
[endif]
[set ui.characterHeightFactor 1.5]
[set ui.characterBaselineY 1.5]
[set character.lavender.imageEffect none]
{{BG_START}}
[textspeed 28]
[autodelay 1650]
[show lavender center happy]
[wait 200]
Lavender: Every tutorial so far taught syntax. This one teaches the habits that keep a project alive past week two.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Naming, structure, writing craft, and the bugs that bite everyone exactly once.

@label lesson_menu
[show lavender far_left talking]
> Naming: files, labels, variables -> section_naming
> Project structure -> section_structure
> Writing craft -> section_writing
> The six most common bugs -> section_bugs
> Quick reference: project hygiene -> quick_reference
> Quiz: spot the problem -> practice_scene
> Back to Tutorial Hub -> return_hub

# ─── Quick Reference ─────────────────────────────────────────────

@label quick_reference
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Good projects are boring to navigate:
narrator: Use stable names: {color=#8888cc}chapter02_rooftop.vns{/color}, {color=#8888cc}trust_lavender{/color}, {color=#8888cc}@label confession_merge{/color}.
narrator: Keep declarations shared, scene scripts focused, and assets sorted by type.
narrator: Validate before playtesting. Commit working milestones. Back up art and audio sources.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Checklist: readable names, shallow folders, one scenario per file, and every branch tested before you build.
> Start the lesson sections -> section_naming
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Naming ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_naming
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: Three naming domains. Same rule for all: {b}the name should explain itself without context{/b}.
narrator: {b}Files:{/b}
narrator: {color=#66bb88}Good:{/color} ch1_rooftop_confrontation.vns, ch2_library_escape.vns
narrator: {color=#ff6666}Bad:{/color} scene3.vns, new_file_FINAL_v2.vns
[show lavender center talking]
narrator: {b}Labels:{/b}
narrator: {color=#66bb88}Good:{/color} rooftop_choice, after_confrontation, ending_brave
narrator: {color=#ff6666}Bad:{/color} label1, temp, here
narrator: {b}Variables:{/b}
narrator: {color=#66bb88}Good:{/color} courage, met_librarian, ch1_route_active
narrator: {color=#ff6666}Bad:{/color} x, flag, val
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Use {b}snake_case{/b} everywhere. Prefix chapter-scoped variables: ch1_courage, ch2_trust.
> Next: project structure -> section_structure
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Project Structure ───────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_structure
[show lavender right talking]
Lavender: A scalable folder layout:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}scripts/chapter_01/{/color} — one .vns file per scene.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}scripts/definitions/{/color} — shared @character, @background includes.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}assets/characters/sprites/{/color} — character art.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}assets/backgrounds/{/color} — scene backgrounds.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}assets/audio/bgm/{/color} — music. {color=#8888cc}sfx/{/color} — effects. {color=#8888cc}voice/{/color} — clips.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/menu/{/color} — menu screens, layouts, styles.
narrator: {color=#8888cc}config/ui/{/color} — dialogue box layout and style.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Rules:
narrator: {b}One scenario per file.{/b} Don't pack multiple scenes into one script.
narrator: {b}Group by type.{/b} Scripts with scripts, art with art, audio with audio.
narrator: {b}Never nest more than 3 folders deep.{/b} Deep trees are hard to navigate.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Test: can a new team member find any file in under 30 seconds? If not, reorganize.
> Next: writing craft -> section_writing
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Writing Craft ───────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_writing
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Technical skill runs the engine. Writing skill makes the player care.
narrator: {b}Two sentences max per dialogue line.{/b} If it fills the text box, split it.
narrator: {b}Read lines aloud.{/b} If it sounds awkward spoken, it reads awkward.
narrator: {b}Give each character a distinct voice.{/b} Vocabulary, rhythm, attitude should differ.
narrator: {b}Use narration for atmosphere{/b}, not for repeating what the player can see.
[show lavender left talking]
Lavender: The golden rule:
narrator: {b}Every line should advance the plot, reveal character, or create mood.{/b}
narrator: If a line does none of those, cut it. The player's time is not free.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: The best VN dialogue sounds like real people talking — not like someone writing dialogue.
> Next: common bugs -> section_bugs
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Common Bugs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label section_bugs
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Six bugs that hit every project. Learn them here instead of in production.
narrator: {b}1. Missing [endif].{/b} Every [if] needs one. The error is silent — wrong branches run and you won't know why.
narrator: {b}2. Typo in [goto] scenario ID.{/b} The script can't find the target. Hard to debug because it fails at runtime, not parse time.
narrator: {b}3. Missing [return].{/b} A [call] without [return] falls through into the next label. Chaos.
narrator: {b}4. Orphaned labels.{/b} A choice points to "park_scen" but the label is "park_scene". One letter.
narrator: {b}5. Untested branches.{/b} You wrote it, but did you click it? There's always one path nobody played.
narrator: {b}6. Variable sprawl.{/b} 100 flags, half undocumented. Simplify before it buries you.
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: All six are caught by one habit: play your own game start to finish before anyone else does.
> Quiz: spot the problem -> practice_scene
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

# ─── Quiz ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@label practice_scene
[set quiz 0]
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Three questions. Let's see if you can spot the issue.

@label pq1
Lavender: Q1: This script has a bug. What is it?
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[if courage >= 3]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: You're very brave.{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}[elif courage >= 1]{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}Lavender: Not bad.{/color}
> Missing [endif] -> pq1_correct
> Missing [return] -> pq1_wrong
> The variable name is bad -> pq1_wrong

@label pq1_correct
[inc quiz]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Right. Every [if] block must close with [endif]. Without it, the engine doesn't know where the block ends.
[jump pq2]

@label pq1_wrong
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Not quite. The block is missing {b}[endif]{/b} at the end. Without it, everything after runs unconditionally.
[jump pq2]

@label pq2
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Q2: What's wrong with this choice target?
narrator: {color=#8888cc}> Visit the library -> libary_scene{/color}
narrator: {color=#8888cc}@label library_scene{/color}
> The label name is misspelled in the choice -> pq2_correct
> The choice text is too long -> pq2_wrong
> Nothing is wrong -> pq2_wrong

@label pq2_correct
[inc quiz]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Exactly. "libary_scene" vs "library_scene" — one missing letter. The engine can't find the target.
[jump pq3]

@label pq2_wrong
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Look again: the choice says "libary_scene" but the label says "library_scene". Typo.
[jump pq3]

@label pq3
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: Q3: You have a greeting used in 5 different scenes. What's the cleanest approach?
> Copy-paste into each scene -> pq3_wrong
> [call] a shared greeting label -> pq3_correct
> Write 5 unique greetings -> pq3_wrong

@label pq3_correct
[inc quiz]
[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Perfect. One source of truth, called from anywhere. Change it once, it updates everywhere.
[jump quiz_result]

@label pq3_wrong
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: The cleanest approach is {b}[call]{/b} — one greeting label, called from all 5 scenes. No duplication.
[jump quiz_result]

@label quiz_result
[show lavender center talking]
[if quiz >= 3]
Lavender: 3/3. Clean instincts. You'll catch these bugs before they ship.
[elif quiz == 2]
Lavender: 2/3. Solid. Review the one you missed — it'll save you a debugging session later.
[elif quiz == 1]
Lavender: 1/3. These are the bugs that eat hours. Worth re-reading the common bugs section.
[else]
Lavender: 0/3. Better to miss here than in production. That's what tutorials are for.
[endif]
> Retake the quiz -> practice_scene
> Back to menu -> lesson_menu

@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_12]
[flag tutorial_done_12]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[goto {{HUB_TARGET}}:topics_page_2]
